specific ethical review requirements. As no material ethical-risk pathway is visible in the paper, no specific ethical weakness is identified, but the absence of a broader ethical discussion is noted as a limitation of the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the MNIST dataset and Google Fonts for training and evaluation. These are widely used public datasets. The text does not explicitly state the specific licensing terms under which these datasets were used, nor does it provide evidence of consent or privacy compliance, although these datasets generally do not contain personally identifiable information. The absence of explicit licensing statements is a minor gap in the documentation of data usage compliance.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The provided paper text includes the full names of the authors (Mehdi Cherti, Balázs Kégl, Akin Kazakci) and their institutional affiliations (CNRS/Université Paris-Saclay, MINES ParisTech) in the header. While this is standard for many publications, it would violate double-blind review policies if such a policy were in effect for the submission. Without a frozen venue policy confirming the anonymity requirements for this specific submission, this cannot be declared a violation, but the presence of identifying information is noted.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work (e.g., Nguyen et al., 2015; Lake et al., 2015) and presents a new experimental framework. There is no visible evidence of textual overlap or uncredited reuse in the provided text. The absence of evidence does not prove originality, but no specific plagiarism concern is observable in the supplied material.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit IRB/ethics approval documentation. The human annotation process described in Section 4.5 involves labeling generated symbols, which is a low-risk activity not typically requiring formal IRB approval. However, the absence of a broader impact discussion or explicit compliance documentation is a gap in the paper's adherence to modern policy expectations for societal considerations.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"c1e9eb82eb8d3f5d3bd02f0cdee3e7f680e393c7caa6d19ccad8e0da8a25212f","paper_id":"ByEPMj5el","paper_ordinal":67,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"999f31c4c867ea84b73c039baa1e16ebea23372abf09c512cfd8c7be1c5806b3","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByEPMj5el","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"1ba6e87a958ec7af6c143f7f06f4f4770bff3168c639e9d4e7284d1ce88a1d42","request_identity_sha256":"9d4bf88ddb4dd32f904744b1c6e7ea97357fd0e84ff5c0bfd022c173a6bb7505","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":863,"prompt_tokens":17859,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18722},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"9d4bf88ddb4dd32f904744b1c6e7ea97357fd0e84ff5c0bfd022c173a6bb7505","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}